<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine port Necochea reopens as swell eases.</title>
<headline>Argentine port Necochea reopens as swell eases.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The major Argentine grain port of Necochea reopened Tuesday after a swell which had kept it closed several days eased, a port official said.</p>
<p>Necochea, in southern Buenos Aires province, reopened at 0530 local time (0830 GMT), and weather forecasts are good for the next few days, the official told Reuters.</p>
<p>A dredger will also have returned the ports main access channel, which had been partially filled with mud, to normal within about 48 hours, the official said.</p>
<p>((--Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
